meta {
  name: Get Heikin Ashi Values
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/heikin-ashi/AAPL?timespan=M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  timespan: M5
  ~sessions: RTH
  ~count: 700
  ~bars: 50
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Get Heikin-Ashi Values

  Converts the symbol's regular OHLC bars into Heikin-Ashi ("average bar") candles so
  you can verify them against the chart. Inspection/analysis only — no orders.

  Heikin-Ashi smooths price: each bar folds into a running average, so trends show as a
  run of same-colour candles with little/no opposite wick.
    HA_close = (open + high + low + close) / 4
    HA_open  = (prev HA_open + prev HA_close) / 2   (first bar seeds with (open+close)/2)
    HA_high  = max(high, HA_open, HA_close)
    HA_low   = min(low,  HA_open, HA_close)

  Any US stock symbol works (the ticker need NOT be in the watchlist).

  ## Timeframes
  Every timeframe the market-data layer serves: native M1/M5/M15/M30/M60/M120/M240 AND
  synthetic minute multiples (M2, M3, …) resampled from M1 transparently. The HA transform
  is timeframe-agnostic.

  ## Query
  - `timespan` — M1/M2/M3/M5/M15/M30/M60/M120/M240/D/W/M/Y (default M1).
  - `sessions` — RTH, PRE, ATH, OVN (default: configured trading sessions).
  - `count`    — bars to fetch back from now (default = warmup-bars). HA is computed over the
                 FULL fetched series so the running average is seeded continuously; only the
                 OUTPUT is trimmed by `bars`.
  - `bars`     — how many most-recent HA points to return (default 50; use 0 for all).

  ## Response (200)
  {
    ticker, timespan, sessions, barsFetched,
    latestHaOpen, latestHaClose, latestColor,
    returned,
    series: [ { timestamp, timestampEt,
                haOpen, haHigh, haLow, haClose, color (GREEN|RED|DOJI),
                open, high, low, close, volume } ]
  }

  Each row carries BOTH the Heikin-Ashi OHLC and the RAW OHLC (+ volume), index-aligned, so
  you can compare the HA candle against the real bar directly. `color` is GREEN when
  haClose > haOpen, RED when below, DOJI when equal.

  ## Verifying against Webull
  Set the chart to Heikin-Ashi on the SAME timeframe and compare on COMPLETED bars. The most
  recent bar may still be forming; if the last value looks off, compare the previous bar. The
  first few HA bars of the fetched series drift until the running average settles (increase
  `count` so plenty of warm-up precedes the day you care about).

  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid session.
  - `502` — Webull market-data error.
  - `503` — no bars returned.
}
